kwin 6.8: finish rendering before a frame goes to the host over wl_shm

On the memfd software device of kwin-6.8-software-shm-presentation.patch there is
no /dev/udmabuf, and llvmpipe only exports native fences where there is one (its
fence export does a full finish first). Without them, endFrame's glFlush only
queues the frame to llvmpipe's rasterizer threads, and the wl_shm buffer is
committed to the host while they still write into it: pixelflux then reads tiles
of the new frame mixed with older content, which shows as flickering rectangles
and UI elements showing through each other.

Finish rendering before committing when frames go to the host as wl_shm buffers,
which is what the udmabuf path already pays through the fence export, and what
kwin's own DRM backend does for llvmpipe. Hosts taking dmabufs are unchanged.

Found by lhns/webtop-nix while carrying the presentation patch.

Applies to kwin 6.8.x after kwin-6.8-software-shm-presentation.patch.

--- a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_egl_backend.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_egl_backend.cpp
@@ -50,6 +50,18 @@ static FormatModifierMap presentableFormats(WaylandBackend *backend)
     return backend->display()->linuxDmabuf()->formats();
 }
 
+// A wl_shm buffer carries no fence: the host reads it as soon as it is committed. The software
+// renderer only exports native fences where /dev/udmabuf exists, and without them glFlush just
+// queues the frame to its rasterizer threads, which then still write the buffer the host reads.
+static void finishRendering(WaylandBackend *backend)
+{
+    if (backend->presentsThroughShm()) {
+        glFinish();
+    } else {
+        glFlush();
+    }
+}
+
 WaylandEglLayer::WaylandEglLayer(WaylandOutput *output, WaylandEglBackend *backend, OutputLayerType type, int zpos)
     : WaylandLayer(output, type, zpos)
     , m_backend(backend)
@@ -133,8 +145,7 @@ bool WaylandEglLayer::endFrame(const Region &renderedDeviceRegion, const Region
         m_query->end();
         frame->addRenderTimeQuery(std::move(m_query));
     }
-    // Flush rendering commands to the dmabuf.
-    glFlush();
+    finishRendering(m_backend->backend());
     EGLNativeFence releaseFence{m_backend->eglDisplayObject()};
 
     // The damage is where the picture changed, and the picture is composed the way the user
@@ -238,8 +249,7 @@ bool WaylandEglCursorLayer::endFrame(const Region &renderedDeviceRegion, const R
         m_query->end();
         frame->addRenderTimeQuery(std::move(m_query));
     }
-    // Flush rendering commands to the dmabuf.
-    glFlush();
+    finishRendering(m_backend->backend());
 
     wl_buffer *buffer = m_backend->backend()->importBuffer(m_buffer->buffer());
     Q_ASSERT(buffer);
